#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:2
msgid "kernel-crypto-api interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `kernel-crypto-api` interface allows access to the [Linux kernel crypto "
"API](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v4.11/crypto/index.html), which itself "
"provides a set of cryptographic ciphers and other data transformation "
"mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:7
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:10
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/kernel-crypto-api-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The kernel crypto API has been designed to be used by any process such that "
"using it requires no special privileges. As this provides a kernel surface, "
"and has a CVE history, this interface needs to be manually connected."
msgstr ""

